{%- doc -%}
  The Tastes Like / Roast info row the 2026 theme migration dropped from individual Brew Guides
  blog articles, placed before the existing main-blog-post section in templates/article.json so
  it sits near the title -- matching sections/article-template.liquid in Shopify theme
  147471433919 ("ONA - OLD 11/26/2025"), the last pre-cutover snapshot, where this info sat
  directly under the heading, above the featured image and article body.

  Split out of sections/brewguide-article-info.liquid (which still carries the brew recipe and
  the cross-sell, both placed after the article body) specifically for this positioning: Codex
  on PR #282 caught that bundling all three pieces into one section placed after main-blog-post
  put the tasting info below the full article body instead of near the title as described, since
  main-blog-post's own block_order (title, details, featured image, content) can't be
  interleaved with a sibling section's content from templates/article.json's "order" array.

  Scoped to the Brew Guides blog only (article.blog.handle == 'brewguides') so it stays inert on
  News/Journal/other blogs that share templates/article.json.

  Metafield types, see reference_shopify_json_string_metafield_no_value:
    - accentuate.tastes_like   string   -> no .value, read directly
    - accentuate.roast         string   -> no .value, read directly
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign is_brewguide_article = false
  if article.blog.handle == 'brewguides'
    assign is_brewguide_article = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if is_brewguide_article -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign tastes_like = article.metafields.accentuate.tastes_like
    assign roast = article.metafields.accentuate.roast

    assign has_info = false
    if tastes_like != blank or roast != blank
      assign has_info = true
    endif
  -%}

  {%- if has_info -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      .section is Horizon's own page-width grid wrapper (assets/base.css): a direct child of it
      is auto-placed in the centred content column with the theme's standard gutters. Without it
      this content would render edge-to-edge against the viewport, since it's a sibling
      top-level section in templates/article.json, not nested inside main-blog-post.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="section">
      <div class="brewguide-article-info">
        {%- if tastes_like != blank -%}
          <div class="brewguide-article-info__row">
            <span class="brewguide-article-info__label">Tastes like</span>
            <span class="brewguide-article-info__value">{{ tastes_like }}</span>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if roast != blank -%}
          <div class="brewguide-article-info__row">
            <span class="brewguide-article-info__label">Roast</span>
            <span class="brewguide-article-info__value">{{ roast }}</span>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .brewguide-article-info {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--gap-sm);
    margin-block-end: var(--gap-xl);
  }

  .brewguide-article-info__row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--gap-sm);
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .brewguide-article-info__label {
    font-size: var(--font-h6--size);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Brew guide article tasting info",
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Brew guide article tasting info"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
